invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_mont64_mul
reason: rsa_mont64_mont_mul's running sum is one limb short, so at the
  largest limb count the top step reads and writes past the array. A
  smaller modulus never shows it. rsa_mont64_mul runs the function at
  that count, where each access is a property.

--- old
    uint64_t t[RSA_MONT64_LIMBS_MAX + 1];
--- new
    uint64_t t[RSA_MONT64_LIMBS_MAX];
